# Frontend Next.js + React/TypeScript Patterns

## Core Principles

- **App Router only**: Build with Next.js App Router (`app/`). Do not add `pages/` routes.
- **Future-first**: Keep only modern Next.js patterns; remove legacy or transitional guidance.
- **TypeScript strictness**: Avoid `any`; prefer explicit types and inferred return types.
- **Material-UI only for UI primitives**: Use Material UI components for form controls, interactive elements, layout blocks, and feedback UI. Do not introduce raw HTML form controls (`input`, `select`, `textarea`, `button`) in `ui/src`.
- **Server-first rendering**: Prefer Server Components for initial data and page composition.
- **Client components for interactivity**: Use `"use client"` only where hooks, browser APIs, or user interaction require it.

## App Router Structure

```txt
ui/src/
  app/
    (pages)/
      page.tsx
      [slug]/
        page.tsx
    (dashboard)/
      page.tsx
      layout.tsx
      loading.tsx
      error.tsx
    api/
      feature/route.ts
    layout.tsx
  components/
  layouts/
    RootLayoutShell.tsx
  styles/
    globals.css
  hooks/
  lib/
  api/
  types/
  utils/
```

## Routing and Directory Conventions (Project-Specific)

- Keep Next.js routing in `ui/src/app/` only (App Router).
- Use `ui/src/app/(pages)/` as the dedicated home for page route files so pages stay separated from shared layout/style files.
- Keep global/root route shell logic in `ui/src/layouts/` (for example `RootLayoutShell.tsx`) and mount it from `ui/src/app/layout.tsx`.
- Keep global styles in `ui/src/styles/` and import them from `ui/src/app/layout.tsx`.
- Do not create `ui/src/pages/` for app content; Next treats it as Pages Router and may create unintended routes.

## Server vs Client Component Rules

### Server Component (default)

- Use async components for initial fetch and view composition.
- Do not use React client hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`) in Server Components.
- Keep secrets, privileged calls, and heavy data fetching on the server.

```tsx
import { getProject } from "@/api/server/projects";
import { ProjectHeader } from "@/components/ProjectHeader";

interface PageProps {
  params: { projectId: string };
}

export default async function ProjectPage({ params }: PageProps) {
  const project = await getProject(params.projectId);
  return <ProjectHeader project={project} />;
}
```

### Client Component (`"use client"`)

- Add `"use client"` only when required for interactivity.
- Keep client islands small and focused.
- Prefer passing ready-to-render data from server to client components.

```tsx
"use client";

import { useState } from "react";
import { Button } from "@mui/material";

export function ToggleDetails() {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
  return <Button onClick={() => setOpen((prev) => !prev)}>Toggle</Button>;
}
```

## Data Fetching Best Practices (Next + React Query)

- **Initial page data**: fetch in Server Components.
- **Client-side mutations**: use React Query `useMutation`.
- **Client-side query sync/live updates**: use React Query `useQuery` only where a client component needs dynamic updates after hydration.
- **Cache coherence**: when mutating, invalidate relevant React Query keys and trigger server revalidation flow where applicable.

### Server Fetch Example

```tsx
import { getItems } from "@/api/server/items";

export default async function ItemsPage() {
  const items = await getItems();
  return <ItemsList items={items} />;
}
```

### Client Mutation Example

```tsx
"use client";

import { useMutation, useQueryClient } from "@tanstack/react-query";
import type { ItemUpdateData } from "@/types/items";
import { apiClient } from "@/api/client";

export function useUpdateItem(itemKey: string) {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: (data: ItemUpdateData) => apiClient.updateItem(itemKey, data),
    onSuccess: () => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["item", itemKey] });
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["items"] });
    },
  });
}
```

## TypeScript Rules

- Do not use `React.FC`; type props directly.
- Do not use `any`; use specific event/types (`SelectChangeEvent`, `unknown`, typed error model).
- Keep domain types in `ui/src/types/`.
- Use discriminated unions for status/state variants.

```tsx
interface ItemCardProps {
  name: string;
  status: "ACTIVE" | "INACTIVE";
}

export function ItemCard({ name, status }: ItemCardProps) {
  return <div>{name} - {status}</div>;
}
```

## Material-UI Usage Rules

- Use MUI components for layout and controls (`Box`, `Stack`, `Card`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`, `FormControl`, `Select`, `Switch`, `Alert`, etc.).
- Prefer `sx` for local styling; extract reusable styling patterns to shared components when repeated.
- Keep `main` and `section` for route-level semantics only; inside forms and interactive UI, use Material UI components exclusively.

```tsx
import { Box, Card, CardContent, Typography } from "@mui/material";

export function SummaryCard() {
  return (
    <section aria-label="summary">
      <Card>
        <CardContent>
          <Typography variant="h6">Summary</Typography>
          <Box sx={{ mt: 1 }}>Content</Box>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>
    </section>
  );
}
```

## Settings Component Template (Inlined)

Use this pattern for settings/edit forms in client components.

### 1) Required Imports

```tsx
"use client";

import { useEffect, useState } from "react";
import {
  Alert,
  Box,
  Button,
  Card,
  CardActions,
  CardContent,
  CircularProgress,
  FormControl,
  InputLabel,
  MenuItem,
  Select,
  TextField,
  Typography,
} from "@mui/material";
import type { SelectChangeEvent } from "@mui/material/Select";
import { Save as SaveIcon } from "@mui/icons-material";
import { useMutation, useQueryClient } from "@tanstack/react-query";
```

### 2) Interfaces

```tsx
interface ItemSettingsProps {
  item: ItemType;
}

interface ItemUpdateData {
  name: string;
  status: string;
  notes: string;
}

interface FormErrors {
  name?: string;
  status?: string;
  notes?: string;
}
```

### 3) Component Structure

```tsx
export function ItemSettings({ item }: ItemSettingsProps) {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  const [formData, setFormData] = useState<ItemUpdateData>({
    name: item.name ?? "",
    status: item.status ?? "ACTIVE",
    notes: item.notes ?? "",
  });
  const [hasChanges, setHasChanges] = useState(false);
  const [errors, setErrors] = useState<FormErrors>({});

  useEffect(() => {
    setFormData({
      name: item.name ?? "",
      status: item.status ?? "ACTIVE",
      notes: item.notes ?? "",
    });
    setHasChanges(false);
    setErrors({});
  }, [item]);

  useEffect(() => {
    const changed =
      formData.name !== (item.name ?? "") ||
      formData.status !== (item.status ?? "ACTIVE") ||
      formData.notes !== (item.notes ?? "");
    setHasChanges(changed);
  }, [formData, item]);

  const validateForm = (): FormErrors => {
    const nextErrors: FormErrors = {};
    if (!formData.name.trim()) nextErrors.name = "Name is required";
    if (!formData.status) nextErrors.status = "Status is required";
    if (formData.notes.length > 5000) nextErrors.notes = "Notes cannot exceed 5000 characters";
    return nextErrors;
  };

  const updateItemMutation = useMutation({
    mutationFn: (data: ItemUpdateData) => apiClient.updateItem(item.key, data),
    onSuccess: () => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["item", item.key] });
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["items"] });
      setHasChanges(false);
    },
  });

  const handleInputChange =
    (field: keyof ItemUpdateData) =>
    (event: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement>) => {
      const { value } = event.target;
      setFormData((prev) => ({ ...prev, [field]: value }));
      if (errors[field]) setErrors((prev) => ({ ...prev, [field]: undefined }));
    };

  const handleSelectChange =
    (field: keyof ItemUpdateData) => (event: SelectChangeEvent<string>) => {
      const value = event.target.value;
      setFormData((prev) => ({ ...prev, [field]: value }));
      if (errors[field]) setErrors((prev) => ({ ...prev, [field]: undefined }));
    };

  const handleSave = () => {
    if (!hasChanges) return;
    const formErrors = validateForm();
    if (Object.keys(formErrors).length > 0) {
      setErrors(formErrors);
      return;
    }
    setErrors({});
    updateItemMutation.mutate({
      ...formData,
      name: formData.name.trim(),
    });
  };

  const handleReset = () => {
    setFormData({
      name: item.name ?? "",
      status: item.status ?? "ACTIVE",
      notes: item.notes ?? "",
    });
    setHasChanges(false);
    setErrors({});
  };

  return (
    <Box component="section" sx={{ p: 3, maxWidth: 800 }}>
      <Typography variant="h6" sx={{ mb: 3, fontWeight: 600 }}>
        Item Settings
      </Typography>

      <Card>
        <CardContent sx={{ p: 3 }}>
          <Box sx={{ display: "flex", flexDirection: "column", gap: 3 }}>
            <TextField
              fullWidth
              label="Name"
              value={formData.name}
              onChange={handleInputChange("name")}
              disabled={updateItemMutation.isPending}
              error={Boolean(errors.name)}
              helperText={errors.name ?? "Enter item name"}
              required
            />

            <FormControl fullWidth error={Boolean(errors.status)}>
              <InputLabel id="status-label">Status *</InputLabel>
              <Select
                labelId="status-label"
                label="Status *"
                value={formData.status}
                onChange={handleSelectChange("status")}
                disabled={updateItemMutation.isPending}
              >
                <MenuItem value="ACTIVE">Active</MenuItem>
                <MenuItem value="INACTIVE">Inactive</MenuItem>
              </Select>
            </FormControl>

            <TextField
              fullWidth
              label="Notes"
              multiline
              rows={10}
              value={formData.notes}
              onChange={handleInputChange("notes")}
              disabled={updateItemMutation.isPending}
              error={Boolean(errors.notes)}
              helperText={errors.notes ?? "Additional notes"}
            />
          </Box>

          {updateItemMutation.isError && (
            <Alert severity="error" sx={{ mt: 2 }}>
              Failed to update settings. Please try again.
            </Alert>
          )}

          {updateItemMutation.isSuccess && !hasChanges && (
            <Alert severity="success" sx={{ mt: 2 }}>
              Settings updated successfully.
            </Alert>
          )}
        </CardContent>

        <CardActions sx={{ p: 3, pt: 0, gap: 2 }}>
          <Button
            variant="contained"
            startIcon={
              updateItemMutation.isPending ? (
                <CircularProgress size={20} color="inherit" />
              ) : (
                <SaveIcon />
              )
            }
            onClick={handleSave}
            disabled={!hasChanges || updateItemMutation.isPending}
          >
            {updateItemMutation.isPending ? "Saving..." : "Save Changes"}
          </Button>

          <Button
            variant="outlined"
            onClick={handleReset}
            disabled={!hasChanges || updateItemMutation.isPending}
          >
            Reset
          </Button>
        </CardActions>
      </Card>
    </Box>
  );
}
```

## Naming & File Conventions

- Components: PascalCase file and symbol names (`UserSettings.tsx`).
- Hooks: camelCase with `use` prefix (`useUpdateStream.ts`).
- Utilities: camelCase file names.
- Route segments in `app/`: lowercase/kebab-case.

## Keep / Remove Guidance

- Keep rules that improve maintainability and fit App Router + strict TypeScript.
- Remove rules that rely on `pages/`, `React.FC`, `any`, or generic React-only conventions that conflict with Next.js server/client architecture.
